-- title:
--   Under unmixedness, if $V \le F_D$ and every prime over $(ps_0) + (V)$ has height at least $|ps_0| + r$, then $2^{r(r-1)/2} u^r h_{(ps_0)+(V)}(uD) \le h_{(ps_0)}(2^r uD)$
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a field, $S$ a commutative $K$-algebra, $B$ a type, and $F$ a family of $K$-subspaces $F_T$ of $S$ indexed by $T \in \mathbb{N}^B$ (a filtration, on which only the hypotheses listed are assumed). Assume that $K$ is infinite, $S$ is Noetherian, $F$ is monotone ($T \le T'$ coordinatewise implies $F_T \subseteq F_{T'}$), $F$ is multiplicative ($a \in F_T$ and $b \in F_U$ imply $ab \in F_{T+U}$) and every $F_T$ is finite-dimensional, and let `hU : UnmixedHeight S`. Let $ps_0$ be a weakly regular list on $S$, $D \in \mathbb{N}^B$, $V$ a $K$-subspace of $S$ with $V \subseteq F_D$, and $r \in \mathbb{N}$, and assume that every prime ideal of $S$ containing $(ps_0) + (V)$ has height at least $|ps_0| + r$. Then for every $u \in \mathbb{N}$, $2^{r(r-1)/2} u^r h_{(ps_0)+(V)}(uD) \le h_{(ps_0)}(2^r u D)$. For an ideal $I$ of $S$, $h_I(T)$ is `boxHilb F I T`, the dimension over $K$ of the image of $F_T$ in $S/I$ (DALAG's $H(I; T)$). A list is weakly regular on $S$ when each entry is a nonzerodivisor on the quotient of $S$ by the ideal generated by the earlier entries (Mathlib's `IsWeaklyRegular`; the final quotient may be zero). For a list $ps_0$, $(ps_0)$ is the ideal generated by its entries and $|ps_0|$ its length. Heights of prime ideals are taken in $\mathbb{N} \cup \{\infty\}$, and $(V)$ is the ideal generated by $V$. The hypothesis `hU : UnmixedHeight S` is assumed here, not proved: it says that for every weakly regular sequence $r_1, \dots, r_k$ of the ring, every associated prime of the quotient by $(r_1, \dots, r_k)$ has height at most $k$. For polynomial rings over a field it follows from Macaulay's unmixedness theorem (DALAG §8.2.1); its formal proof is planned for C1.2 of the Diaz modulus mission. The names `boxHilb`, `blockBox`, `torusBox`, `torusIdeal`, `torusList`, `torusReduced`, `boxD`, `torusCoeffPoly`, `torusPoint` and `UnmixedHeight` are those of the published Definition `DiazHilbertBox` (module `Definitions.Def_DiazHilbertBox`).
--
--   **Proof.** `DiazModulus.exists_isWeaklyRegular_append_of_height` gives $r$ elements $P_0, \dots, P_{r-1}$ of $V$ such that $ps_0$ followed by them is weakly regular, and `DiazModulus.isSMulRegular_quotient_of_isWeaklyRegular_append` turns this into the chain condition: $P_k$ is regular on $S/((ps_0) + (P_j : j < k))$. Each $P_k \in V \subseteq F_D$, so `DiazModulus.boxHilb_chain_bound` gives $2^{r(r-1)/2} u^r h_{(ps_0)+(P)}(uD) \le h_{(ps_0)}(2^r uD)$. Finally $(ps_0) + (P) \subseteq (ps_0) + (V)$, and the Hilbert function is antitone in the ideal (`DiazModulus.boxHilb_anti`).
--
--   **Novelty.** Not found in the sources read in this form; routine. A finite-level form of DALAG Th. 8.8 (through Th. 8.4), with unmixedness and the heights as hypotheses.
-- source:
--   Finite-level form of M. Waldschmidt, Diophantine Approximation on Linear Algebraic Groups, Grundlehren der mathematischen Wissenschaften 326, Springer, 2000, Th. 8.8 (§8.3.1, p. 239) and Th. 8.4 (§8.2.3, p. 236), the step that gives (8.21) in §8.4.1 (p. 246); Chapter 8 is by D. Roy. Not found in the sources read in this form; routine. Uses DiazModulus.isSMulRegular_quotient_of_isWeaklyRegular_append, DiazModulus.exists_isWeaklyRegular_append_of_height, DiazModulus.boxHilb_chain_bound and DiazModulus.boxHilb_anti. C1.1 of the Diaz modulus mission. Formal proof: Diaz modulus mission, 29 October 2026 (C. Perassi).

import Definitions.Def_DiazHilbertBox

namespace DiazModulus

theorem boxHilb_le_of_height {K S B : Type*} [Field K] [CommRing S] [Algebra K S] [IsNoetherianRing S] [Infinite K]
    (F : (B → ℕ) → Submodule K S) (hFmono : Monotone F)
    (hFmul : ∀ {Tₑ Uₑ : B → ℕ} {aₑ bₑ : S}, aₑ ∈ F Tₑ → bₑ ∈ F Uₑ → aₑ * bₑ ∈ F (Tₑ + Uₑ))
    (hFfin : ∀ Tₑ, FiniteDimensional K ↥(F Tₑ))
    (hU : UnmixedHeight S)
    (ps₀ : List S) (hps₀ : RingTheory.Sequence.IsWeaklyRegular S ps₀) (D : B → ℕ)
    (V : Submodule K S) (hV : V ≤ F D) (r : ℕ)
    (hH : ∀ p : Ideal S, p.IsPrime → Ideal.ofList ps₀ ⊔ Ideal.span (V : Set S) ≤ p →
      ((ps₀.length + r : ℕ) : ℕ∞) ≤ p.height) (u : ℕ) :
    2 ^ (r * (r - 1) / 2) * u ^ r * boxHilb F (Ideal.ofList ps₀ ⊔ Ideal.span (V : Set S)) (u • D)
      ≤ boxHilb F (Ideal.ofList ps₀) ((2 ^ r * u) • D) := by
  sorry

end DiazModulus
